SIMPLE  =                    T / conforms to FITS standard                      BITPIX  =                    8 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    0 / number of array dimensions                     EXTEND  =                    T                                                  VERSION =                  1.2 / file format version                            XCENTER =               1023.5 / DM centre along X in pixels                    YCENTER =               1023.5 / DM centre along Y in pixels                    PIXSIZE =               0.0125 / pixel size (meters)                            PUPM    =                  8.0 / nominal pupil diameter (meters)                PITCHM  =                  0.2 / DM pitch (meters)                              COMMENT The DM FITS file is compatible with COMPASS DM database.                COMMENT     The primary header contains the keywords:                           COMMENT     * PIXSIZE : the size of the pixels on the maps in meters.           COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     * XCENTER, YCENTER are the coordinates of the centre of the pupil, eCOMMENT xpressed in pixels, in a reference frame conformable to (i,j) coords. ThCOMMENT e translation from pixels to meters can be done using:                  COMMENT         meters = (pixels - XCENTER) * PIXSIZE                           COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     * PUPM is the diameter of pupil stop (meters).                      COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     * Additionally the header provides the user with:                   COMMENT         PITCHM is the size of the DM pitch in meters (may be handy is soCOMMENT me cases and useful when using this file with COMPASS software)         COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     This FITS file contains 3 extensions:                               COMMENT     * Extension 'I1_J1' are the coordinate (i,j) of the first pixel for COMMENT each of the 2D maps (see Extension 2), so that they can be inserted in aCOMMENT  larger map.                                                            COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     * Extension 'INFLU' are the 2D maps of the influence functions.     COMMENT                                                                         COMMENT     * Extension 'XPOS_YPOS' are the coordinates (xpos, ypos) of the  phyCOMMENT sical location of the actuator, in pixels. This data is provided for infCOMMENT ormation only and does not directly participate to build the DM. The preCOMMENT sent coordinates are positions in M1 space, i.e. include the distorsion COMMENT due to telescope optics.                                                END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             XTENSION= 'IMAGE   '           / Image extension                                BITPIX  =                   32 / array data type                                NAXIS   =                    2 / number of array dimensions                     NAXIS1  =                 1377                                                  NAXIS2  =                    2                                                  PCOUNT  =                    0 / number of parameters                           GCOUNT  =                    1 / number of groups                               EXTNAME = 'I1_J1   '           / extension name                                 END                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                             